  "description": "Supervises the Litestream sidecar from inside your .NET app: restores the SQLite database from its replica on startup (if the local file is missing) and continuously streams the write-ahead log to S3/GCS/Azure/file storage for the life of the process, via a hosted background service. Pairs with Rask.SQLite's WAL default, which Litestream requires. Register with `services.AddRaskSqliteLitestream(...)` and call `RestoreSqliteFromLitestreamAsync()` before opening the database. Requires the `litestream` binary on the host (or a path you configure). Standalone: depends only on the Microsoft.Extensions hosting/DI abstractions.",
